  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), throttle seen from the rear-left and above, grip's outboard end (end dial) towards the camera, control panel in front of the grip, flaps/MVR lever to the right of the grip",
  "mappingSource": "Virpil support sheet \"VPC VMAX Prime Throttle\" (Button Mapping, https://support.virpil.com/en/support/solutions/articles/47001263912-vpc-vmax-prime-throttle, attachment 47301892852) confirms the catalog's source, the EDCD map 33448196.buttonMap (https://github.com/EDCD/EliteCustomButtonNames/blob/main/files/INTO%20Bindings/DeviceButtonMaps/33448196.buttonMap); panel labels B1-B6, B7, T1-T5, E1/E2, APU, MODE 1-5 are printed on the panel",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "keyboard keys: sheet inset = 23 24 25 in the row next to the KEYBOARD label, 26 27 28 in the row towards APU; the printed B5/B6 labels are legible on the photo and agree. the grip's thumb face points away from the camera (only two controls stick out edge-on on the right silhouette and cannot be told apart), the index face with the 4-way index hat and the middle-finger button faces away too. hat direction names: the sheet draws the index hat as 7 top / 5 bottom / 6 left / 8 right and the thumb hat as 22 top / 19 right / 20 bottom / 21 left; the catalog (EDCD) calls them 5/6/7/8 and 19/20/21/22 = up/right/down/left. Same cyclic order, only the reference \"up\" differs - not a numbering conflict. the 2-way hat (10 push, 11/13) is drawn left/right on the sheet (13 left, 11 right) with optional 12/14 (dashed); the catalog calls 11/13 up/down.",
